## Lore

The Gromek are winged giants from another dimension, a world of towering mountains that they conquered outright long ago. With a beast-like head, wide-set eyes, a fanged maw, horns, a ridge of bony plates from snout to crown and a pair of vast bat wings, they are regularly taken for demons, which they are not. Nobody knows how they reached the Palladium World; since they turned up in the Baalgor region, where so many other aliens also appeared, the Elf-Dwarf War is the usual suspect.

Their whole society is built around war. Males train as warriors from the age of five. Females raise the young and work as smiths and crafters, and they also learn to fight, serving as healers and strategists; the sexes hold equal standing and scouting parties are split evenly between them. Gromek are fine weaponsmiths, live in clans of about eighty to a village, and reserve what compassion they have for their own kind. Stranded explorers found a hidden base, grow a tribe, and then set about subduing everything around it.

They once held the Mount Nimro region, until the giants there united and threw them out. The Gromek have sworn to wipe the giants out in return, and the war has settled into a bloody stalemate in the Baalgor Mountains, where flight lets Gromek clans raid from peak to peak. A few warlords there now take tribute from everything nearby and rule small kingdoms on the inner edge of the range.

**Alignment:** Any, but mostly selfish or evil.

**O.C.C.s available:** Any optional or Men of Arms O.C.C., clergy, or Men of Magic. Mercenary, soldier, ranger, knight and palladin are favoured. Priests are uncommon because a Gromek rates very few gods as deserving of devotion, and although mages are rare, a typical clan still has a Wizard or Warlock or two. No psionics.

**Physical Appearance:** Big, powerfully built and alarming to look at: horns, scales, a mouthful of pointed teeth, and leathery wings. The sexes are hard to tell apart; a female is usually no taller than eight feet.

**Size:** 8 to 10 feet tall (2.4 to 3 m). **Weight:** 600 to 800 pounds (270 to 360 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 180 years.

**Languages:** Their own, spoken and written. Most also speak Giantese.

**Enemies:** Humans and most native intelligent peoples; giants above all.

**Allies:** Ogres, trolls and giants at times, less often as the quarrel with giantkind deepens. The peoples of the north, Wolfen included, are strangers to nearly all Gromek.

**Habitat:** Mountains and high hills in moderate to hot climates. The largest settlements are in the Baalgor Mountains; some are found in the Yin-Sloth Jungles and the wild parts of the Land of the South Winds.

## GM Notes

Pairs normally stay together for life, and a Gromek''s loyalty runs to kin, comrades and the race as a whole. Pregnancy lasts twelve months and yields one or two young. Boys start combat training by five; girls start on holistic medicine, literacy and strategy, with physical training from seven. Adulthood comes at thirteen for females and sixteen for males.

The smallest clan or scouting group holds 2D6 warriors, half of them female. Where the Gromek dominate, dozens of villages may cluster together, thousands strong.

Loot can be anything taken in conquest, but what a Gromek actually prizes is well-made arms and armor. Enchanted weapons are the one kind of magic a warrior will carry; other magic items are handed to wizards and priests. Between half and three quarters of a tribe''s hoard sits in a cache whose location the leader shares only with a deputy, and the balance is held by the priest, or by the wizard in a clan without one. For a small or medium clan, figure 500 to 2,000 gold in coin and valuables, 2D4 common magic items, and several dozen good weapons and suits of armor.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gromek');


